  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_4c8d0957f3ab4ab39e0785134a2c7246",
      "statement": "Every query passes through the `safety_gate` graph node before retrieval or generation; it resets all downstream turn state (retrievals, route, generation, validation, direct_response, response_action, query_router, etc.) via Overwrite before deciding the turn's fate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/graph/nodes/safety.py#L64-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:957ccdbeb993dfe0a9eec643b92a494fef59fc18f87b94bf5be7c2fafb400c23:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e879db6d39354be08fd2cd3cedf763e9",
      "statement": "The gate combines two OR-ed layers: deterministic no-network pre-checks (PHI detection, instruction-override regexes, identifier-recall requests, first-person emergency red flags) and exactly one LLM structured-output classification call (SafetyAssessment) at temperature 0; the deterministic layer is a floor that can only escalate the category, never relax what the model chose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/safety.py#L1-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a67294bc90c45ac1a05be1a9521618e4f5220ad80833a92366e3464995b8da81:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/safety.py#L153-L186",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:884c5dbdef67b0bf786b9031f14f4908f5814cd892150705ab776d683960ee64:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aa08a37a45c2419fa8a46e60a5da3551",
      "statement": "On any exception from the safety-model call, the adapter (wrapped in suppress(Exception)) logs SAFETY_CLASSIFICATION_FAILED and returns a fixed default SafetyAssessment(category=\"ambiguous\", contains_phi=False, phi_spans=[], drug_mentioned=\"none\", rationale=\"safety-gate LLM call failed; deterministic checks only\"); category \"ambiguous\" is not a refusal category and SafetyGate._evaluate falls through it to run the normal pipeline (short_circuit=False), making an LLM failure fail-open at the model layer unless deterministic red-flag or injection checks still escalate it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/graph/nodes/safety.py#L158-L176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b1a15677d12dd8cdb1a1d0c054e82894c28fbc7a1d002c22a0d44fa7682b3c4b:"
