        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_34c748278c694ac1b9be49265055f93d",
      "statement": "Corrupted or stale-template-version boundaries are parsed as inert and effectively dropped by RefusalBoundary.from_state (which rejects any response not in the current allowed_responses set), so corrupted checkpoint state can never widen behavior beyond the fixed template set; turning the gate off (HC_RAG_SAFETY_GATE=false) never writes and never replays a boundary; same-thread concurrent turns are unsupported by design and the CLI/eval harness run turns sequentially.",
      "evidence": [
